  "term": "arrest reaction",
  "definition": "Arrest reaction is the change in brain electrical activity measured during the transition between closing and opening the eyes. In this context, it is used as an EEG-based test of alpha and theta oscillations across repeated eyes-closed/eyes-open trials.",
